        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            There is no such thing as a certified low histamine protein powder, so the best choice is the one with the fewest, freshest ingredients: an unflavored whey isolate if you tolerate dairy, or a single-ingredient pumpkin seed, rice or hemp powder if you do not. Skip bone broth, collagen, fermented proteins, probiotics, cocoa and superfood blends while you are testing.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Introduce one powder at a time, drink shakes fresh, and treat any restricted diet as a short experiment rather than a permanent rule. If symptoms are severe, persistent or unexplained, see a doctor or allergist before cutting out more foods.
